Commit 4e9d037f1cfc8e29efcb1f67bc668e06ff2b6643 of CPython's 3.15
branch, the backport of commit 8eb3d2c1c41ca7ce628554413981c1eb763a1494
of main, which fixes CVE-2026-124249. http.cookiejar applies an expired
Set-Cookie to the jar before it asks the cookie policy: the header's
Domain and Path name the stored cookie to delete, so a response from one
host can delete the cookies of another domain in a shared jar. The patch
asks CookiePolicy.set_ok() first, as RFC 6265 section 5.3 requires. The
3.15 branch holds the fix; no release does, and 3.15.2 does not.

